{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra","id":947366,"title":"Killing a Vampire from/on the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T18:06:11-07:00","id":947366,"title":"Killing a Vampire from/on the Umbra","content":"So I run a mixed Vampire and Werewolf game on Sundays, using the Vancouver Dark Alliance product, one of my players who I figured is decently versed in Werewolf, I am still newish to the game but I understand the basics and am reading more and more as I go, but I am far more used to Vampire.<br /> Can a werewolf, who has sidestepped into the Umbra, see his opponents as they were on the physical realm and thus just attack them without them being able to defend themselves and thus you have a vampire who was JUST fighting a Crinos formed werewolf who used sidestep and all of a sudden he just gets ripped apart because he was destroyed on the umbra? is this a thing?<br /> <br /> Secondly, I have been told, though I dont really believe it that the sun is ever present even at night on the Umbra and thus a Vampire on the Umbra can be destroyed, I might have misheard this and he might have been referring to a specific realm within the Umbra but either way, can a Gurahl force a Vampire from the physical realm INTO this &quot;magical&quot; Umbra place in order for the vampire to explode due to Sun.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the player seems to think he can just step sideways to avoid a fight (which is sucky but can happen) and then due to being able to just see the Vampires &quot;true form&quot; on the umbra, just turn around, side step back and launch a surprise attack.<br /> The player later said he heard these things were a thing from a 3rd party person who he thought knew alot about werewolf, my concern about this players mastery of knowledge was suspect to begin with.<br /> Ive since put an end at least temporarily to that Umbra shenanigans till I can determine it was legit or not.<br /> Any help is greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting, I put a post on the White Wolf Reddit requesting help as well, and they showed me a lot of things. I just want to cast my net wide to make sure I have as much information going forward.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all your help.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:29:24-07:00","id":947381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra#post947366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I run a mixed Vampire and Werewolf game on Sundays, using the Vancouver Dark Alliance product, one of my players who I figured is decently versed in Werewolf, I am still newish to the game but I understand the basics and am reading more and more as I go, but I am far more used to Vampire.<br /> Can a werewolf, who has sidestepped into the Umbra, see his opponents as they were on the physical realm and thus just attack them without them being able to defend themselves and thus you have a vampire who was JUST fighting a Crinos formed werewolf who used sidestep and all of a sudden he just gets ripped apart because he was destroyed on the umbra? is this a thing?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, there are several layers to the Umbra. When a werewolf &quot;steps sideways&quot; into the spirit world, he's entered the Penumbra, which is a spiritual reflection of the real world. There are thematic differences in the Penumbra, but at its core it's pretty similar. The werewolf would no longer be able to see people, though. Old buildings or trees, sure... but not transient things like parked cars or a moving person. It takes a long time for something to establish a reflection there. The werewolf could &quot;peek&quot; across the gauntlet (the boundary between the two realms), but it's difficult and he'd just be able to see across for a turn. No ability to interact without some sort of extra fetish (werewolf spiritual artifacts) or high-level gifts (werewolf disciplines)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra#post947366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, I have been told, though I dont really believe it that the sun is ever present even at night on the Umbra and thus a Vampire on the Umbra can be destroyed, I might have misheard this and he might have been referring to a specific realm within the Umbra but either way, can a Gurahl force a Vampire from the physical realm INTO this &quot;magical&quot; Umbra place in order for the vampire to explode due to Sun.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, this is the opposite of correct. It is always night in the Penumbra. The stars and celestial bodies are each their own distant spirit realm, though... and even if they are visible in the sky, it would not count as a real sun as far as I know. It's just not the same stuff. Depending on the timeline of your game, if the End Times have started, there may also be an Anti-Sun (Anthelios) star shining in the night sky. Again... should be no issue for a vampire, if he -somehow- got in there.<br /> <br /> Again, there are some rare Gifts that let you interact with things through the Gauntlet, but almost all of them are well out of reach of a starting character. Also, there's literally only one or two very specific powers that would allow you to bring anything other than the Garou and his ritually dedicated possessions across. So if he steals a kewl ninja sword and wants to go into the Umbra, it clatters to the floor and gets left behind. Depending on how nice you are as a ST, the same might be said of the cash he just took out of the ATM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra#post947366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, the player seems to think he can just step sideways to avoid a fight (which is sucky but can happen) and then due to being able to just see the Vampires &quot;true form&quot; on the umbra, just turn around, side step back and launch a surprise attack.<br /> The player later said he heard these things were a thing from a 3rd party person who he thought knew alot about werewolf, my concern about this players mastery of knowledge was suspect to begin with.<br /> Ive since put an end at least temporarily to that Umbra shenanigans till I can determine it was legit or not.<br /> Any help is greatly appreciated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually true... to a limited extent. A werewolf could step into the Umbra as their action... it's not a simple or reflexive action, though. They roll Gnosis against a difficulty of the Gauntlet (the barrier between realms; it's harder in cities and easier in the wilderness. In the city it's probably an 8 or so if I remember right.) If they get 3 successes, they hop right over. 2 success and it takes 30 seconds. 1 success and it's FIVE MINUTES to cross... so while they might pop out of existence on this side, they're not about to spring any clever maneuvers without getting 3 successes to cross in both directions. Also, there are spirits in the spirit realm. There's just as much chance he'd cross over and run into something nasty on the other side. Also, botching a roll to cross is VERY bad news if you don't have werewolf buddies to help you.<br /> <br /> Edit: It should also be stressed that once across, he can't see the Vampire anymore without making another Gnosis roll to &quot;peek&quot;, or hoping it hasn't moved since he left. Also, Gnosis is incompatible with Rage (barring some extremely rare exceptions), so he can't use Rage for extra actions (or anything else) during a turn he rolls or spends Gnosis. And vice versa (so no Rage for extra actions and activating a Fetish during the same turn either).<br /> <br /> Some Werewolf writers like the Umbral Ambush tactic. Other writers of the game hate it and discourage it. Overall, it's still a generally valid tactic..,. but again, most evil things' lairs attract evil spirits who like to bask in the evil mojo. So sneaking in from the Umbra is often just as dangerous or moreso, depending on the location and what lives there.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps... if I missed any points, point them out and I can explain more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:48:32-07:00","id":947389,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, its appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:49:20-07:00","id":947390,"title":"","content":"Ok, I haven't read W20, so my info might be dated. But for the most part Crusher-of-Cities info is correct. The part that's not accurate, to my knowledge, is the Umbral Sun. In the Prenumbra day and night cycle just like the physical realm. The thing is that day time is the Garou's enemy. At night, due to Luna and various Incarna, friendly spirits of the Garou come out at night. Its during the daylight in the Umbra that the banes and other nasties come out. Speaking of banes, there is a good chance there might be one or two following the player Vampires around, especially if their Humanity is like 5 or lower. And just a little side note for the ST, a Garou may DRAG someone into the Umbra. The Garou physically grabs hold,of the person and roles THE GAROU's Gnosis. What ever result happen a to the both of them. That's how whole packs quickly Step Sideways. They let the Theurge, who should have the highest Gnosis, drag the pack threw the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:49:25-07:00","id":947391,"title":"","content":"A Werewolf can peek into the real world from the Umbra, but it takes a successful Gnosis roll (difficulty is Gauntlet rating, in a city this is most likely 7). It is not automatic and may fail. While the Garou peeks into the Realm, he is totally ignorant about what is happening in the Umbra. The Realm appears shadowy and monochromatic. You can't make out fine details.<br /> <br /> You cannot attack someone on the other side of the Gauntlet though. If you are in the Umbra, you cannot attack someone in the Realm, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Nor can you pull someone into the Umbra unless you have the appropriate Gift.<br /> <br /> The Umbra has the normal change between day and night. The sun is not present though. I think there is daylight, but I don't think the sun itself ever appears (I could be wrong, this is from memory). The moon, however, does appear, and you can see its phases. Whether this counts as real sunlight is up to you as the ST.<br /> <br /> Crossing the Gauntlet does carry some risk and is not automatic. If you have three or more successes (rolling your Gnosis), the time is instantaneous. Two successes means you take 30 seconds to cross over. One success means 5 minutes. You can't do anything else when this happens, like defend yourself from an attack. Failure means you don't cross over and need to wait an hour before you can try again. A botch means he is &quot;caught&quot; which means the Garou is trapped in an interdimensional prison zone. Physical beings don't see him, but anything in the Umbra realizes what has happened and can attack him. Another Garou can attempt to save such a trapped Garou, but if that fails the trapped Garou is lost forever.<br /> <br /> So it is a very dangerous maneuver in the fight because if you don't get three or more successes, you can easily get killed. You also need to determine whether a reflective surface is required for the attempt. That is required in every edition except Revised. If so, it might be very hard to step sideways in a fight because the Garou likely is not really concentrating on such a surface.<br /> <br /> Plus you can always decide that a Vampire with Auspex or something else may get a feeling or something that helps it with being surprised even if the crossing is instantaneous.<br /> <br /> I always consider stepping sideways to be the equivalent of going on a vision/spirit quest. It is not really designed for the kind of tactical combat you are talking about, although some of the things are possible (like trying to escape, or entering the Realm from the Umbra with intent to attack once you cross over).<br /> <br /> So overall, I don't think your friend is correct. He has many details wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:54:09-07:00","id":947393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947390#post947390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I haven't read W20, so my info might be dated. But for the most part Crusher-of-Cities info is correct. The part that's not accurate, to my knowledge, is the Umbral Sun. In the Prenumbra day and night cycle just like the physical realm. The thing is that day time is the Garou's enemy. At night, due to Luna and various Incarna, friendly spirits of the Garou come out at night. Its during the daylight in the Umbra that the banes and other nasties come out. Speaking of banes, there is a good chance there might be one or two following the player Vampires around, especially if their Humanity is like 5 or lower. And just a little side note for the ST, a Garou may DRAG someone into the Umbra. The Garou physically grabs hold,of the person and roles THE GAROU's Gnosis. What ever result happen a to the both of them. That's how whole packs quickly Step Sideways. They let the Theurge, who should have the highest Gnosis, drag the pack threw the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as a Werewolf you can grab the Prince of a city, drag him to the Umbra and leave him there? Can Vampires get back or are they trapped there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:55:08-07:00","id":947394,"title":"","content":"The question intrigued me, so I asked a friend of mine with more experience in this field than myself. He said a werewolf being able to see the vampire on the Umbra requires a power to see the material world from the Umbra as vampires don't have an Umbra state. So the whole thing about attacking a vampire's &quot;true self&quot; isn't working due to there not being something to attack. <br /> <br /> If you drag a vampire into through the Gauntlet and in the presence of the Sun on the Umbra then they would die, but the sun is not ever present so it requires some set up. Also while dragging one the kindred through the Gauntlet is possible it is a serious pain in the neck and it's far easier to just shoot the vampire to death, or since the first question involved Chrinos using Chrinos to murder it.<br /> <br /> As far as ambushes go, possible but tricky. As he put it &quot;It's like a shark arguing how easily it can kill a camel. The camel is not in the water so no matter how good you are at swimming it's not going to make the camel more vulnerable&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:58:48-07:00","id":947396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947390#post947390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, And just a little side note for the ST, a Garou may DRAG someone into the Umbra. The Garou physically grabs hold,of the person and roles THE GAROU's Gnosis. What ever result happen a to the both of them. That's how whole packs quickly Step Sideways. They let the Theurge, who should have the highest Gnosis, drag the pack threw the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to take someone else into the Umbra (without one of the specific rites or gifts) a few conditions must be met. 1) They must have the natural ability to cross the gauntlet. 2) They must be a packmate. 3) They must be willing.<br /> <br /> ALL THREE CONDITIONS must be met to lead someone into the Umbra. (Source: W20 pg 309-310. And as far as I know this rule is identical in all editions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:01:00-07:00","id":947397,"title":"","content":"When ever a Garou pulls someone threw the Gauntlet, if they do not have their own way across or the Garou pulls them back threw, their marooned. I do believe that there MIGHT be a Thaumaturgy Path that can help a Vampire cross back. I would have to do some research on it lol. As far as the Umbra goes with the Vampires, they are in trouble. Vampires with Humanity scores less then 7 are considered Wyrm tainted. They are detected with Sense Wyrm Gift, Gaia spirits fear/hate them. Banes love them. And in the Umbra the Vampire will starve. Ephemera is not Vitae. Vampires do not get nourishment from ephemera. And 99% of the Umbra is ephemera","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:05:43-07:00","id":947404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947390#post947390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part that's not accurate, to my knowledge, is the Umbral Sun. In the Prenumbra day and night cycle just like the physical realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was, indeed incorrect. The Penumbra has night and day, and during the day sunlight is &quot;omnipresent&quot;, meaning you don't have to have line of sight to the &quot;sun&quot; for it to reach any given location. The Umbra book also confirms on page 10 that this sunlight WOULD affect a vampire if it somehow found itself in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where my idea of perpetual night came from. Might be an earlier edition thing... I've been playing since 1st. Or I'm just crazy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:05:59-07:00","id":947405,"title":"","content":"As I stated I haven't read W20, and I don't remember those conditions in the earlier editions, but I could be very wrong. Its been some years since I read a WtA book in depth. That situation bout &quot;snatching foes to Umbra&quot; didn't come up often enough to matter in my Chronicle lol. In my opinion the OP should use the conditions listed by Crusher above.Your thing bout the perpetual night is like my pulling threw the Gauntlet thing lol. I have been playing since 1st also","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:09:09-07:00","id":947407,"title":"","content":"Oh heres a related issue can a garou &quot;Kill&quot; a vampire or psychichs astral projection or is it just not possible to reach it, is the &quot;Astral plane&quot; basicly the umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:26:01-07:00","id":947420,"title":"","content":"No, I think that they are technically part of the Periphery. And a werewolf has much better methods of hunting down and killing a critter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:35:28-07:00","id":947427,"title":"","content":"From my understanding of the Umbra, there is a High Umbra that is the domain of the Intellectual concepts. Its there that Astral Projection takes place. Technically a Garou could kill a person Projecting. But first he would have to leave the Prenumbra, travel threw the Umbra into the High Umbra, then find the Astral Projection. So in theory, yea a Garou can kill a Vampire Projecting. Is it worth the effort? That is up to the Garou in question lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:42:45-07:00","id":947484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947391#post947391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...lots of stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a bunch of misinformation floating around the thread. If you want to go by the books, everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said is correct.<br /> Garou can Peek into the material from the Umbra, but can't see the Umbra at the same time (without Gifts). Vampires cannot be pulled across without specific Gifts. Sunlight should affect them normally in the Umbra. No they generally don't have a way back (or anything to eat).<br /> <br /> On the question of Astral Projection and the Umbra. That is a lot more of a gray area. It depends on how you set up your cosmology. The various Penumbras may or may not be the same and different based on perception. So it is up to you (or the ST) to decide what the Astral Plane is and how it interacts with Garou (and Wraiths, Changelings, etc.). Unfortunately this is part of the hurdle to overcome when playing a crossover game.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm not sure if W20 or M20 clarified the Astral Plane thing. I'm fairly certain V20 didn't care so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:57:42-07:00","id":947545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947391#post947391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always consider stepping sideways to be the equivalent of going on a vision/spirit quest. It is not really designed for the kind of tactical combat you are talking about, although some of the things are possible (like trying to escape, or entering the Realm from the Umbra with intent to attack once you cross over).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I believe as well. The Umbra is a really cool concept and I think that using it for combat advantages cheapens the specialness of the Umbra. Even if the rules allowed for some of these tactics I wouldn't allow it because I don't think that they are thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:57:08-07:00","id":947567,"title":"","content":"Between umbra 20 and mage 20 Vampire astral projection is clarified as being in the High Umbra, and Garou take damage entering the High Umbra equal to their rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:00:23-07:00","id":947570,"title":"","content":"Just my additional thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. Umbra revised is the only book that mentions that it is bright for a werewolf during daytime in the umbra. All other books (mainly the core books of the series) state that it was dark, since garou can't see the sun. How Helios-related shifters would perceive the situation is not describes. I'd go with Umbra revised, all the time.<br /> <br /> 2. Peeking isn't limited to a turn, if successful. At least I have no indication that it was not lasting as long as the garou concentrates. But it is dangerous since the garou can't perceive the penumbra any more, that is spirits, beings that are there and inanimate ephermal objects and landscape. Unless the garou takes damage, spirits might be able to surround the garou and call for backup, as loud as they want. I guess, some other instances will end peeking to, falling from a cliff for example, or being knocked prone or other forced alterations to movement. So, the garou wouldn't realise someone is collaring him, but once the leash is pulled he stumbles and chokes and that he would probably realise, even if it doesn't add to actual damage.<br /> As far as affecting the material world from the umbra goes: the earliest gift allowing for that is from Book of Auspices and it is a level two gift. Unlike discipline levels, a garou needs to have accomplished something to be allowed to learn level two gifts, but level two is fairly early. Although the gift has some limitations as to how high the gauntlet in the area where the attack occurs may be, it is a decent assassination gift.<br /> The most recognised gift to do such an attack allows for claw usage and is level 4 for one specific tribe and a couple of other werebeasts. This is really uncommon, I'd say. Especially if compared to the level two gifts which can only be used with a knife or handmade weapon (although, I guess if you can hand-craft a nuclear device it counts; also fetish-weapons may be handmade, like a Fang Dagger). The 'Spirit Knife' is available to all shamans, which is one in five werewolves approximately and knife damage plus crinos strength is still a fairly high amount of lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:04:55-07:00","id":947592,"title":"","content":"Honestly if a Garou player wants to take out a vampire with little no chance of it fighting back there's a much easier method. Just kill them in their haven during the day. You have bunch of tracking powers, and the umbra thing dosn't require as much shenanigans to pop and out of to gank someone who's asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:18:41-07:00","id":947602,"title":"","content":"On the taking a vamp into the umbra. The ONLY way i have ever heard of that being done was with a Gurhal rending the gauntlet and TOSSING one in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:47:31-07:00","id":947607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947602#post947602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the taking a vamp into the umbra. The ONLY way i have ever heard of that being done was with a Gurhal rending the gauntlet and TOSSING one in...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a level 3 gift for Theuge and Children of Gaia characters that can allow to take other people into the umbra, with the garou.<br /> If you rule that an undead is more like an object and less like a person and that the gift wasn't applicable, then there still is the level 4 gift to bring items one can carry into the umbra for Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> It is open to debate if a vampire could also come into the umbra, if the Gauntlet was zero at one point. This is the case at a caerns heart, but can also be replicated with other means, like the &quot;key to the Umbra&quot; fetish, that lowers the local gauntlet by one per activation success.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:44:44-07:00","id":947668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947602#post947602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the taking a vamp into the umbra. The ONLY way i have ever heard of that being done was with a Gurhal rending the gauntlet and TOSSING one in...</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, though, the Gurahl rending is also a Level 1 Rite, not an innate ability. So unlike stepping sideways where the Garou goes &quot;poof&quot; and then we wait to see how long until he reappears in the penumbra, for the Gurahl rite he has to stand there ripping at the Gauntlet for anywhere from a turn to five minutes, depending on successes. The way the rite is written, the normal crossing time is shared between rending and crossing. Also, while not the case in the past, W20 Changing Breeds now adds that only werebears can cross through it. In the past it simply stated &quot;closes immediately after the Gurahl crosses through&quot;... though again, as written, the act of rending and crossing seems to be combined into one action. I don't think the Gurahl could open a portal, step away to grapple someone while it's still open, and then return to chuck them through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947607#post947607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is open to debate if a vampire could also come into the umbra, if the Gauntlet was zero at one point. This is the case at a caerns heart, but can also be replicated with other means, like the &quot;key to the Umbra&quot; fetish, that lowers the local gauntlet by one per activation success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would generally rule that with a Gauntlet of 0 the two worlds are co-located, but I wouldn't consider anyone to have 'crossed' into the other once the gauntlet rises again. But as you said, I don't think that's directly clarified anywhere. Also, I think the Nuwisha can bring a person into the Umbra, while a fetish like the Whole Gym Bag or a Ratkin gift also can bring inanimate objects. It's a short list of things that can do it... but yeah, there are a couple ways.<br /> <br /> I forget which book states it... maybe Umbra?... but I believe if someone is brought into the Umbra without the natural ability to enter or exit, they eventually become some type of weak spirit rather than simply die or starve to death. But that takes a long, long time... like days/weeks/months... and it's basically the same as dying, since weak gafflings are really only semi-sentient. That said, this bit of trivia might also be 1st or 2nd edition... so who knows if it's still supposed to be true. A lot of authors prefer to pretend the &quot;Samuel Haight&quot;-era of books never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Edit: Fixed the information about Gurahl rending 08-10-2016, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:44:07-07:00","id":947761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947668#post947668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would generally rule that with a Gauntlet of 0 the two worlds are co-located, but I wouldn't consider anyone to have 'crossed' into the other once the gauntlet rises again. But as you said, I don't think that's directly clarified anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more interesting question for me is, what happens when a person actively leaves an area where both are co-located. Meaning a human is at a spot in the world where the gauntlet is zero, i.e. in a forest clearing. He then sees something &quot;strange&quot; (as in a spirit), he would normally not see and decides to follow that being. His intent is to leave this place on the penumbra side of the Gauntlet. If intent is an contributing factor in (pen-)umbral travel, then the human might just be on the other side of the Gauntlet when he leaves the scene for a place where there actually is a Gauntlet..<br /> <br /> Stuff like this may very well be the source of some fairy tales about strange worlds, humans might get trapped in. (Aside from similar places where the access to the Dreaming is possible, instead of the middle Umbra).<br /> <br /> <br /> The process of becoming a spirit is called &quot;Disconnecting&quot; and it is iirc only detailed for garou. If they don't enter the Umbra, the difficulty for stepping sideways increases by 1 per year. If the increase reaches 10 they are considered a spirit. There are actual Silent Strider NPCs in the books who turned spirits in that way and are therefore the closest the Striders have to Ancestors. Also, a week (I think) of sustenance is equal to one temp Gnosis, so Garou can survive quite a bit in the umbra.<br /> <br /> I think it is never detailed for beings other then garou (and by extension several fera). My guess is, that such a person could eat parts of the umbral landscape to get sustenance, as well as spirits. I mean, if such a person could kill a animal spirit gaffling, it could be eaten. If they are in a penumbral-equivalent of a grocery store, then there might be something resembling food there. But starving would be the most likely scenario. That is, unless the person makes it into a realm, where per definition other rules might apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:28:59-07:00","id":948002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947668#post947668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind, though, the Gurahl rending is also a Level 1 Rite, not an innate ability. So unlike stepping sideways where the Garou goes &quot;poof&quot; and then we wait to see how long until he reappears in the penumbra, for the Gurahl rite he has to stand there ripping at the Gauntlet for anywhere from a turn to five minutes, depending on successes. The way the rite is written, the normal crossing time is shared between rending and crossing. Also, while not the case in the past, W20 Changing Breeds now adds that only werebears can cross through it. In the past it simply stated &quot;closes immediately after the Gurahl crosses through&quot;... though again, as written, the act of rending and crossing seems to be combined into one action. I don't think the Gurahl could open a portal, step away to grapple someone while it's still open, and then return to chuck them through.</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation in question, was the DM let the player of the bear-folk, rend, allowed everyone else to run through, and the gurahl to toss in 2 leeches we had tied up, then he stepped through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:50:24-07:00","id":948022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948002#post948002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The situation in question, was the DM let the player of the bear-folk, rend, allowed everyone else to run through, and the gurahl to toss in 2 leeches we had tied up, then he stepped through.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rite specifically says now that it shouldn't have worked that way. But since it was allowed, that part really doesn't matter. Once you allow Vampires into the Umbra, you almost completely enter houseruling territory since that isn't a place they should end up. Whether or not the sun burns them is completely up to the ST (I don't see a reason it shouldn't). There won't be anything to eat (aside from the Changers) so the Vampires are slowly going to tick through their blood points. Personally I would rule that the Curse of Caine prevents them from disconnecting and that they will eventually end up in torpor if they don't find a way out. And Rending the Gauntlet only works from the material, so I'm not sure entirely sure how you <i>could </i> get them out without bringing them through an open Caern (not going to happen) or getting the assistance of another entity (powerful spirit, a mage, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:20:59-07:00","id":948062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947761#post947761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is never detailed for beings other then garou (and by extension several fera). My guess is, that such a person could eat parts of the umbral landscape to get sustenance, as well as spirits. I mean, if such a person could kill a animal spirit gaffling, it could be eaten. If they are in a penumbral-equivalent of a grocery store, then there might be something resembling food there. But starving would be the most likely scenario. That is, unless the person makes it into a realm, where per definition other rules might apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's been detailed in about a paragraph or two's worth of text somewhere.... but for the fastest confirmation that this actually is a thing, W20 pg 165 under 'Grasp the Beyond': &quot;If left in the Umbra too long, living beings turn into spirits entirely.&quot; I'll look for the longer version detailing poor humans that get left in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Edit: Umbra, pg 10. Garou can live off Gnosis while in the spirit world, but any being without that trait finds nourishing food hard to come by (obviously). If the spirit of the &quot;foodstuff&quot; gives itself willingly, it might provide some nutrition... but there are no guarantees. Once that being starves to &quot;death&quot; they instead become a spirit. Humans often become ephemera. Animals - their respective animal spirit. This even applies to Garou, who typically become ancestor spirits.<br /> <br /> This appears next to the block about penumbral sunlight, and reinforces how immensely screwed Vampires in particular are in the umbra. Unless they brought humans with them to feed on, or can strike a deal with a Blood spirit (highly unlikely), they will certainly starve... and that's only if they can somehow survive the shadowless daytime of the penumbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 08-10-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:47:41-07:00","id":948079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947761#post947761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more interesting question for me is, what happens when a person actively leaves an area where both are co-located. Meaning a human is at a spot in the world where the gauntlet is zero, i.e. in a forest clearing. He then sees something &quot;strange&quot; (as in a spirit), he would normally not see and decides to follow that being. His intent is to leave this place on the penumbra side of the Gauntlet. If intent is an contributing factor in (pen-)umbral travel, then the human might just be on the other side of the Gauntlet when he leaves the scene for a place where there actually is a Gauntlet..</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thing happens in the Wild West- the Storm Eater obliterates the Gauntlet and spirits wander out of the umbra and mortals or animals wander in. Often the creatures from this world die, but sometimes they become corrupt spirit-hybrid things called stormborn that follow the Storm Eater around and take advantage of the shattered Gauntlet to prey on weak Gaian spirits or hapless humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:12:20-07:00","id":948096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947545#post947545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I believe as well. The Umbra is a really cool concept and I think that using it for combat advantages cheapens the specialness of the Umbra. Even if the rules allowed for some of these tactics I wouldn't allow it because I don't think that they are thematically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several splats that prefer to assassinate targets or otherwise attack them in this manner, so I'm going to have to call foul on this standpoint. Stepping sideways and sneaking around to hit them from behind is not just okay with spirits (including the spirit of the game), many of them <b>explicitly endorse</b> <b>it</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:02:21-07:00","id":948153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948096#post948096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are several splats that prefer to assassinate targets or otherwise attack them in this manner, so I'm going to have to call foul on this standpoint. Stepping sideways and sneaking around to hit them from behind is not just okay with spirits (including the spirit of the game), many of them <b>explicitly endorse</b> <b>it</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both camps have managed to find their way into the writer-pool. Several books (and one notable species of Fera) endorse this as an everyday tactic and a basic combat maneuver. Meanwhile at least one edition of the Umbra book explicitly condemns crossing the Gauntlet for anything short of a full-blown epic questline set to span months of gameplay. It sucks, but it's not like we've ever pretended like the books have any semblance of continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:37:05-07:00","id":948195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948096#post948096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are several splats that prefer to assassinate targets or otherwise attack them in this manner, so I'm going to have to call foul on this standpoint. Stepping sideways and sneaking around to hit them from behind is not just okay with spirits (including the spirit of the game), many of them <b>explicitly endorse</b> <b>it</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are entitled to their opinion, but I don't see it that way. I might allow it under certain conditions, but I wouldn't want it to be a common tactic or one that is used frivolously. I certainly wouldn't want players taking down an important villain by just attacking them from the Umbra and not having a real fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:45:13-07:00","id":948200,"title":"","content":"The information I was saying bout the High Umbra was from Rage Across The Heavens and from the Book of Worlds. Now mind you, it has been 10+ years since I have read those books and also I have not read W20 or M20. Either could have updated or even changed what I have said. In the end, no matter what the books have said it like what Idpersona said &quot;its up to the ST...&quot; It is all bout you and your troupe having fun and enjoying the game<br /> <br /> Edit: and,it seems somehow I have missed a entire page of this post....my post could well be irrelevant....sorry if,it is<br /> <br /> By the way, Mages can also become Disconnected to from staying in the Umbra. And Disconnection happens faster in the Deep Umbra. As far as I can remember from Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 08-10-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:00:43-07:00","id":948210,"title":"","content":"Rules for people becoming spirits after staying in the Umbra too long can be found, apart from Werewolf, in any Book of The Umbra of Mage, (and I guess in M20 too). It's a thing for other beings. Also, some beings are immune to this phenomenon, notably Marauders and Nephandi, and a few other weirdos.<br /> <br /> However, vampires are never mentioned in these rules, and while that means that the ST has to rule about disembodied vampires, I have a strong reason to think that they should have a special consideration regarding this rule. Vampires can live indefinitely in the Dark Umbra, as prooven by the sect known as the Tal'mahe'Ra, that has a few members who live in the shadow of Enoch(in one the Far Shores of wraith, a part of the Umbra nevertheless).<br /> <br /> It's also stated that vampires can't find sustenance in wraiths without a rare form of Necromancy, and even then, sucking from ghosts doesn't replace the fresh blood of the living. Since wraiths are very similar to Spirits in their &quot;composition&quot; (Plasma being very related to Ephemera), I would say that there's reasons to think they would sufer from hunger problems if they don't leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:12:47-07:00","id":948216,"title":"","content":"As for whether or not the Umbra can be a radical tool, doesn't matter. The ST decides that. I personally use it as a ST for both radical and epic quests. The Umbra is a highly dangerous place, even the Preumbra. If the players want to take the risk as using it tactically that's fine by. But there ls all kinds of nasties that wouldn't appreciate a Garou mucking around their territory. Its all a matter of interpation on how you want the Umbra to be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:40:12-07:00","id":948232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948195#post948195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are entitled to their opinion, but I don't see it that way. I might allow it under certain conditions, but I wouldn't want it to be a common tactic or one that is used frivolously. I certainly wouldn't want players taking down an important villain by just attacking them from the Umbra and not having a real fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Keep in mind, the Umbra around a vampire is usually swimming with frustrated banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:11:39-07:00","id":948260,"title":"","content":"In terms of what happens to a vampire brought into the Penumbra and abandoned there, one thing that could very well happen is that a Bane comes by and agrees to move the vampire back to the Realm - but in exchange the vampire has to perform certain acts of Chiminage (do specific kind of evil acts once he's back in the real world). A vampire arriving in the Penumbra probably &quot;disturbs the Force&quot; and all sorts of Banes realize that and go looking for it.<br /> <br /> Very often we are told in the books that Banes hang out in areas where there are vampires, because vampires do all sorts of things the Banes like. This means there could very well be Banes well placed to observe any trans-umbral fight between Garou and vampire.<br /> <br /> In fact, this is probably another good reason why this strategy should not be done. While a Garou is in the midst of fighting a vampire, a Bane or group of Banes could very well ambush him. Choosing such tactics in a city environment is probably not wise, as the urban umbrascape is generally not conducive to a Garou. Of course, out in the wilderness it works more in the Garou's favor, but very few vampires will be found there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:49:33-07:00","id":948291,"title":"","content":"Considerng it is said in the VtM books that any Kindred with a Humanity under 7 can be detected with Sense Wyrm Gift, its almost a sure bet that at least a few Banes will be stick close to a Kindred. And in my opinion if a Kindred was marooned in the Penumbra and a Bane decided to help, i don't tho,i Chiminage it would want. Instead it would more likely want to Possess the Kindred. Type of Possession that results in Formori. Just my two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T21:09:23-07:00","id":948334,"title":"","content":"Kindred possession is a complicated thing.<br /> <br /> Also, it's worth saying that most banes couldn't actually transport the Vampire back (though for story purposes this can of course change). They will claim they can in making deals for their immediate gratification, but actually doing it might be a bit more complicated. And banes are for all intents and purposes demons. Making deals with them should go about as well as you would think. Almost any bane capable of transporting a vampire across the gauntlet is going to be far older (and more cunning) than the vampire it's dealing with. Punching a hole through the gauntlet is no small task.<br /> But yea. Banes are demons (lower case). Making deals with them is effectively infernalism. Have fun with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:05:13-07:00","id":948361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948022#post948022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite specifically says now that it shouldn't have worked that way. But since it was allowed, that part really doesn't matter. Once you allow Vampires into the Umbra, you almost completely enter houseruling territory since that isn't a place they should end up. Whether or not the sun burns them is completely up to the ST (I don't see a reason it shouldn't). There won't be anything to eat (aside from the Changers) so the Vampires are slowly going to tick through their blood points. Personally I would rule that the Curse of Caine prevents them from disconnecting and that they will eventually end up in torpor if they don't find a way out. And Rending the Gauntlet only works from the material, so I'm not sure entirely sure how you <i>could </i> get them out without bringing them through an open Caern (not going to happen) or getting the assistance of another entity (powerful spirit, a mage, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC the group just LEFT him there.. As we continued on our way to our main goal.. Getting into the main area of a group of vampires to take them out... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948260#post948260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of what happens to a vampire brought into the Penumbra and abandoned there, one thing that could very well happen is that a Bane comes by and agrees to move the vampire back to the Realm - but in exchange the vampire has to perform certain acts of Chiminage (do specific kind of evil acts once he's back in the real world). A vampire arriving in the Penumbra probably &quot;disturbs the Force&quot; and all sorts of Banes realize that and go looking for it.<br /> <br /> Very often we are told in the books that Banes hang out in areas where there are vampires, because vampires do all sorts of things the Banes like. This means there could very well be Banes well placed to observe any trans-umbral fight between Garou and vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the DM had several banes at the main vamp haven area, but had none following the mook pair we took out and left in the penumbra... Not sure though if he ever though OF having some of those banes materialize into the prime to help the leeches beat us, or jsut had them there to potentially ambush any of us who side stepped to get OUT of there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:24:11-07:00","id":948376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948334#post948334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And banes are for all intents and purposes demons. Making deals with them should go about as well as you would think. Almost any bane capable of transporting a vampire across the gauntlet is going to be far older (and more cunning) than the vampire it's dealing with. Punching a hole through the gauntlet is no small task. But yea. Banes are demons (lower case). Making deals with them is effectively infernalism. Have fun with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep to all of that. But it's not like the vampire really has any choice if the other option is death. A powerful jaggling is probably needed to cross the Gauntlet, but that's not too hard. Once a Gaffling Bane finds one, the news goes up pretty quick.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:25:09-07:00","id":948378,"title":"","content":"Lets not forget that cause of the nature of Vampires there would be a good chance that what would be following, lured to or found near a vampire could be corrupted pattern spiders. Or other corrupted Weaver spirits. I a cam see a Vampire being conned into becoming a Drone if it's trapped in the Umbra and wanting a way out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:45:41-07:00","id":948446,"title":"","content":"So from the jist of what Ive been reading, here is the conclusions I have come to.<br /> <br /> -Werecreatures have no way to bring a Vampire over to the Umbra, barring specific gifts, GRASP THE BEYOND (level 4) seems to be one.<br /> -In order to go over with a werecreature, it must be a member of the pack, have the innate ability and be WILLING.<br /> -Werecreatures CANNOT by default see anything, that isnt semi permanent once over in the Penumbra WITHOUT Peeking? Even then its shadowy and hard to discern beyond shapes.<br /> -Vampires have no UMBRA form while standing on the physical plane, though Banes may be attracted to it?<br /> -A werecreature CANNOT grapple a Vampire and Step Sideways with it, forcing it wholey onto the Umbra.<br /> -A Vampire that somehow manages to find his way to the Umbra, will likely die of Sunlight as its everywhere long before starvation. Unless he can get to the Dark Umbra fast, like where the Tal'mah're are.<br /> - A werecreature can step sideways, assuming he makes the rolls, PEEK assuming he makes the rolls, move, Sidestep back to advantageous ambush location and launch an attack, unclear whether he can set up extra attacks through Gnosis usage while on the Umbra.<br /> -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","user":"Avalon2099","date":". 08-11-2016, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:05:30-07:00","id":948492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948232#post948232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Keep in mind, the Umbra around a vampire is usually swimming with frustrated banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, any page reference for that ?<br /> I can see, that a long-time haven or place where vampires regularly hunt becomes tainted and banes like it there an come there to regain Essence, but by no means are banes &quot;swimming&quot; around any random vampire. At least not that I ever read that...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:23:56-07:00","id":948505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Werecreatures have no way to bring a Vampire over to the Umbra, barring specific gifts, GRASP THE BEYOND (level 4) seems to be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within W20 rules. There was in resived a gift on level 3 to bring a person, while the gift you describe is for an object. W20 allows both with the level 4 gift.<br /> I would argue, that a vampire is a person, despite being undead, therefore in revised the level 3 gift would be enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-In order to go over with a werecreature, it must be a member of the pack, have the innate ability and be WILLING.</div> </div> </div> </div>Special rules might apply if a werecreature is member of a pack, doesn't have the ability to step sideways itself, but the pack uses the &quot;Opener of ways&quot;-Rule to have the whole pack stepping sideways. Hengeyokai has rules for that, but I don't recall them in detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Werecreatures CANNOT by default see anything, that isn't semi permanent once over in the Penumbra WITHOUT Peeking? Even then its shadowy and hard to discern beyond shapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, possibly less so with more successes. However, it is written, that smell and sound are easier to perceive than light while peeking and that garou can track by smell (in lupus form) a person on the other side of the gauntlet by means of peeking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Vampires have no UMBRA form while standing on the physical plane, though Banes may be attracted to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A werecreature CANNOT grapple a Vampire and Step Sideways with it, forcing it wholey onto the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The level 4 gift explicitly states, that an unwilling person gets a Willpower roll, subtracting successes from the gift users attempt to step sideways.<br /> The same was true for the revised-era level 3 gift, iirc.<br /> But forcing a person onto the other side of the Gauntlet is possible under these circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A Vampire that somehow manages to find his way to the Umbra, will likely die of Sunlight as its everywhere long before starvation. Unless he can get to the Dark Umbra fast, like where the Tal'mah're are.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Umbra-book states, that places that are in essence dark are excepted from the 'omnipresent sunlight' rule. That is a cave or something like that, that is naturally always dark.<br /> Also, there is no easy travel from the middle umbra to the dark umbra. Such a task, while maybe possible would require a long travel from the penumbra deeper into the umbra to a realm that overlaps middle and dark umbra to then emerge there. This is somewhat theoretical and by no means a way to survive....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A werecreature can step sideways, assuming he makes the rolls, PEEK assuming he makes the rolls, move, Sidestep back to advantageous ambush location and launch an attack, unclear whether he can set up extra attacks through Gnosis usage while on the Umbra.-</div> </div> </div> </div>The stepping sideways, peek, move, step sideways method can get one into ambush location. Since stepping sideways, peeking and so on are all separate actions, it would take several rounds. I don't remember Gnosis allowing for additional attacks, anywhere...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:51:39-07:00","id":948570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from the jist of what Ive been reading, here is the conclusions I have come to.<br /> <br /> -Werecreatures have no way to bring a Vampire over to the Umbra, barring specific gifts, GRASP THE BEYOND (level 4) seems to be one.<br /> -In order to go over with a werecreature, it must be a member of the pack, have the innate ability and be WILLING.<br /> -Werecreatures CANNOT by default see anything, that isnt semi permanent once over in the Penumbra WITHOUT Peeking? Even then its shadowy and hard to discern beyond shapes.<br /> -Vampires have no UMBRA form while standing on the physical plane, though Banes may be attracted to it?<br /> -A werecreature CANNOT grapple a Vampire and Step Sideways with it, forcing it wholey onto the Umbra.<br /> -A Vampire that somehow manages to find his way to the Umbra, will likely die of Sunlight as its everywhere long before starvation. Unless he can get to the Dark Umbra fast, like where the Tal'mah're are.<br /> - A werecreature can step sideways, assuming he makes the rolls, PEEK assuming he makes the rolls, move, Sidestep back to advantageous ambush location and launch an attack, unclear whether he can set up extra attacks through Gnosis usage while on the Umbra.<br /> -</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly correct. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> seems to have covered all of this with more detail.<br /> <br /> There are other Gifts that can affect how all of this works as well, but they are specific exceptions to the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:40:21-07:00","id":948631,"title":"","content":"on a side note just some extra info...the Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook on page 197 does state under Obfuscate that its effects do not reach into the Penumbra. So if a werewolf peeks from the Umbra they are able to see vampires using Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":".  I figured I'd toss this bit in, just in case it was of interest, since it is a mixed game. 08-11-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:23:32-07:00","id":948805,"title":"","content":"I remember reading that banes more then likely will be found in the presence of vampires and following them around. It wasn't a actual crunch statement though. But considering that any Vampire with a Humanity lower than 7 regeristers as Wyrm from Sense Wyrm it is a good chance that there will be at least one bane in the presence of a Vampire and stalking it in the Umbra. And as a side note, very spiritual and/or emotional persons do have a slight Penumbra shadow/image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:26:11-07:00","id":948807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948805#post948805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading that banes more then likely will be found in the presence of vampires and following them around. It wasn't a actual crunch statement though. But considering that any Vampire with a Humanity lower than 7 regeristers as Wyrm from Sense Wyrm it is a good chance that there will be at least one bane in the presence of a Vampire and stalking it in the Umbra. And as a side note, very spiritual and/or emotional persons do have a slight Penumbra shadow/image.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says different things in different places. Umbra Revised took strides to sever most of the comings and goings of vampires from anything having to do with the Umbra on account of how spiritually dead Kindred are.<br /> <br /> (I think I just internalized something from the misty recesses of time in the post above, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:35:25-07:00","id":948814,"title":"","content":"It is true that Kindred are spiritually void, but that doesn't change that the actions of the Kindred drawing Banes to it. And I imagine a bane or two would be smart enough to notice that there is something causing all the &quot;free food&quot; and just following the source around. It wouldn't be a long stretch IMO if a herd member might even become a Formori eventually. But in the end its what the ST feels what will feel right and fit into his Chronicle. Personally I believe they purposely left Vampires from most Umbra stuff and spirits around them and interacting to keep the two titles separate. I never understood why they haven't wrote a book dealing solely with cross over guides and rules. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 08-11-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:37:59-07:00","id":948815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948446#post948446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from the jist of what Ive been reading, here is the conclusions I have come to.<br /> <br /> -Werecreatures have no way to bring a Vampire over to the Umbra, barring specific gifts, GRASP THE BEYOND (level 4) seems to be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't just vampires. No one but anything not in the garou's pack. So no doing it to ghouls, Mortals, changelings whatever else is in your game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -In order to go over with a werecreature, it must be a member of the pack, have the innate ability and be WILLING. </div> </div> </div>The Rites that created MultiBreed packs allow breed that have it innately to lead other willing members of the pack into the Umbra even if they don't have it innately. Generally the rites to do this are unknown by the Garou nation but are currently available to to the Ahdi and Emerald Courts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Werecreatures CANNOT by default see anything, that isnt semi permanent once over in the Penumbra WITHOUT Peeking? Even then its shadowy and hard to discern beyond shapes. </div> </div> </div>There are gifts for seeing bothsides at the same time. The Umbra is a spiritual Shadow of the material, it will be related but not 1 for 1. More emotional investment makes things more effective. But there are car spirits etc. Over all its complicated. Travel through the umbra isn't meant to be an easy way to cut around things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Vampires have no UMBRA form while standing on the physical plane, though Banes may be attracted to it? </div> </div> </div>No sapient being has an umbral form. You can't attack ANYTHING just from the umbra(Vampires, mages, other changers etc). Banes might be attracted to where vampires gather depending on how wyrmy they are and what wyrmy stuff they do.. For example a Sabbat pack's communal haven where they occasionally do blood feasts is going to be pretty Baney.<br /> <br /> A Camarilla Elysium may be less so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -A werecreature CANNOT grapple a Vampire and Step Sideways with it, forcing it wholey onto the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Presuming no specialized Gift, correct. This is equally true of anything else it would want to attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -A Vampire that somehow manages to find his way to the Umbra, will likely die of Sunlight as its everywhere long before starvation. Unless he can get to the Dark Umbra fast, like where the Tal'mah're are. </div> </div> </div>That depends on what's available. a Gangrel might still be able to earth meld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - A werecreature can step sideways, assuming he makes the rolls, PEEK assuming he makes the rolls, move, Sidestep back to advantageous ambush location and launch an attack, unclear whether he can set up extra attacks through Gnosis usage while on the Umbra.<br /> - </div> </div> </div>Lets use an example, George the Garou wants to kill Vinny the vampire. Vinny is sitting at his desk doing boring nightly influence up keep things so this is the perfect time to jump him alone.<br /> <br /> George uses the umbra. Now presumably since effort has been put into defense on the material plane you might have all manner of security based entity slowing George down so don't treat the Umbra as Teleport.<br /> <br /> But he gets to where he thinks vinny is.. he Peeks and vinny is there at his desk having a long conversation! Lucky George. George prepares to attack he makes his step sideways roll and it takes 5 minutes.<br /> <br /> Vinny has long since finshed the Call and left the room to go feed for the night.. poor George.<br /> <br /> Now lets assume George rolled better. He rolled enough to get there in 30 seconds. Vinny is still talking! George gets a single surprise attack before we go into rounds because you can't spend Rage in the same turn as you step sideways.<br /> <br /> Now instead lets pretend George brought his pack.. well unless Vinny's a serious elder this is a foregon conclusion, but really would he have much of a chance even without the surprise?<br /> <br /> Conversely a bunch of assamites with silver would ruin George's day while he's sitting at the bar in a very quick fashion... Ambushes are awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:41:07-07:00","id":948820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948815#post948815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely a bunch of assamites with silver would ruin George's day while he's sitting at the bar in a very quick fashion... Ambushes are awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember cubs, get disguise Gifts. Doppelganger is great, obviously, but even Man's Skin has its uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:20:22-07:00","id":948897,"title":"","content":"You guys are ALL awesome! Thank you so much for helping me flesh this all out, I was super hesitant on running a game with both included before, now I feel much better knowing how I can meld the two.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Rites that created MultiBreed packs allow breed that have it innately to lead other willing members of the pack into the Umbra even if they don't have it innately. Generally the rites to do this are unknown by the Garou nation but are currently available to to the Ahdi and Emerald Courts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can this be done with Garou and NON-Garou/Werecreatures? I plan to run a mixed pack scenario where the Neonates meet up with the Garou and they either kill each other or get along, and if they get along could they qualify for something like this? A quest to reach the aforementioned places where its offered and the inherent dangers of such would be present of course, but is it remotely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:46:17-07:00","id":948904,"title":"","content":"You could always Houserule it and have the Garou able to anyone through the Guantlet by having it be 2 success harder to cross. Meaning that anything less then 3 success is failure, 4 success is 5 mins, 5 success is 30 sec, and 6 success is instant. Allows it to be done but keep a the gifts that do it relevant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T16:15:03-07:00","id":948916,"title":"","content":"Or you could pull a MacGuffin and just give them access to a custom fetish that opens an actual portal/gateway into the Umbra. Maybe charge the user a Gnosis point per use or per person to prevent abuse... and there you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:37:01-07:00","id":949063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948897#post948897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys are ALL awesome! Thank you so much for helping me flesh this all out, I was super hesitant on running a game with both included before, now I feel much better knowing how I can meld the two.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Rites that created MultiBreed packs allow breed that have it innately to lead other willing members of the pack into the Umbra even if they don't have it innately. Generally the rites to do this are unknown by the Garou nation but are currently available to to the Ahdi and Emerald Courts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can this be done with Garou and NON-Garou/Werecreatures? I plan to run a mixed pack scenario where the Neonates meet up with the Garou and they either kill each other or get along, and if they get along could they qualify for something like this? A quest to reach the aforementioned places where its offered and the inherent dangers of such would be present of course, but is it remotely possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally not since Vampires lack any real connection to gaia, and the garou would probably be taking a renown hit for hanging out with wyrm creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:39:23-07:00","id":949064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon2099</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=948897#post948897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can this be done with Garou and NON-Garou/Werecreatures? I plan to run a mixed pack scenario where the Neonates meet up with the Garou and they either kill each other or get along, and if they get along could they qualify for something like this? A quest to reach the aforementioned places where its offered and the inherent dangers of such would be present of course, but is it remotely possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the books, not really.<br /> But don't let that stop you. Make it up yourself if you feel it would serve the story. Use the idea set forth by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12162_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12162\" data-vbnamecard=\"12162\">Crusher-of-Cities</a> and have it be a unique fetish, or create a &quot;lost&quot; Rite for the players to discover. Rending the Gauntlet (which shouldn't work) is level 1. Just say there is a level 3 or 4 (depending on your player's highest Rituals rating) rite that can work the way you need it to.<br /> <br /> It certainly goes against canon (100%), but so does your story seemingly and the players are okay with it and presumably having fun. Do what you need to do to tell the story you want to tell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:33:09-07:00","id":949539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=947404#post947404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where my idea of perpetual night came from. Might be an earlier edition thing... I've been playing since 1st. Or I'm just crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall there being something in the original Werewolf 1st edition's corebook about the moon effectively being the sun of the Umbra, and things being like a moonless night during the day. That sounds like something that later got changed what with the inclusion of planetary spirits and Helios and such.<br /> <br /> At any rate, odds are if you're grappling with a vampire during daylight hours you've already found its haven and gotten past all the defenses thereof. Seems like it'd be a lot easier to just kill it while it's sluggish than stepping sideways and dragging it into the Middle Umbra for sunbathing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:29:23-07:00","id":949681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947366-killing-a-vampire-from-on-the-umbra?p=949539#post949539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall there being something in the original Werewolf 1st edition's corebook about the moon effectively being the sun of the Umbra, and things being like a moonless night during the day. That sounds like something that later got changed what with the inclusion of planetary spirits and Helios and such.<br /> <br /> At any rate, odds are if you're grappling with a vampire during daylight hours you've already found its haven and gotten past all the defenses thereof. Seems like it'd be a lot easier to just kill it while it's sluggish than stepping sideways and dragging it into the Middle Umbra for sunbathing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It persisted as far as Hengeyokai, when any time in the Umbra around Beast Courts territory was effectively day, and actual day had one main sun and nine smaller ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}